  "deny": [
    {
      "from": "internal/chatsync",
      "to": "internal/chat",
      "reason": "settled decision 7: chatsync is a leaf. internal/chat pulls in ~47 internal packages (config, agent, contextstate, workspace, ...). The only use was chat.TurnErrorMessage; it is injected as ProjectorOptions.ErrorMessage instead."
    },
    {
      "from": "internal/chatsync",
      "to": "internal/tools",
      "reason": "settled decision 7: chatsync is a leaf. tools.RedactToolArgs() is process-global mutable state (an atomic.Bool), so reading it here makes any test of gate composition mutate a package global. The host passes the decision as ProjectorOptions.RedactToolArgs instead."
    },
    {
      "from": "internal/storage",
      "to": "internal/context/manager",
      "reason": "persistence package importing a domain policy package; the shared usage types moved to internal/usage (see internal/storage -> internal/usage)"
    }
  ],
  "description": "Internal import edges: an allowed-edge baseline, a hard edge-count cap, and a deny-list that overrides the baseline. Re-baselined at 400 measured edges after the UI replacement Phase 1 added internal/tui/adapter. The prior cap of 400 was set after the SDK convergence Stage 0 Item 4 split (slices 1-6: cliworktree, cliagents, cliorchestrate, cliworkflow, clichat) of the former 44-out-degree internal/cli. Phase 1 added the uiadapter edge pair (uiadapter -> internal/agent, uiadapter -> internal/tui/kit/uievent), pushing 398 -> 400. Phase 2 added uiadapter -> internal/chat to wrap *chat.Session in ports.Conversation / ports.TurnHandle; the discovered-during-implementation edges (provider, uikit/intent, uikit/ports) took 400 -> 404. Phase 3 added 10 edges for the build constructor: 7 from internal/tui/adapter to composition-root packages (composition, config, hooks, mcp, redact, storage, workspace), plus 2 from internal/tui/adapter extracted as helper signatures during the gate-driven refactor (contextstate, tools), plus 3 from cmd/mivia-ui (uiadapter, config, provider) for the --demo=false real-harness path. Measured count 404 -> 416, edge cap 405 -> 420 leaving 4 edges of headroom for the Phase 4+ wiring (settings ports, approver, MCP server selection from config). B.0.5 added internal/sdkadapter with 7 edges to bridge package-shape mismatches between the CLI types and the SDK types (provider, tools, skills, hooks, contentref, reasoning, ledger); measured count 416 -> 420 baseline, edge cap 420 -> 430 leaving 10 edges of headroom for Phase 4+ sdkadapter edges plus the Phase 5+ bundle and pipeline work. B.2 #3 dropped internal/contentref (the migration moved every caller to internal/sdkadapter); the 7 contentref edges from sdkadapter, ledger, agent, agentmsg, clichat, coordinator, remainder vanish, measured count 420 -> 413, cap stays at 430. C.1 added internal/hooks/session, a leaf package (config, hooks) that owns lifecycle-hook session state so internal/tui/adapter can reach /hooks listing without depending on internal/cli: 4 edges (cli -> hooksession, hooksession -> config, hooksession -> hooks, uiadapter -> hooksession); measured count 407 -> 411 (scripts/check_import_layers.py is authoritative for the running count; this note may drift from it), cap stays at 430. D.1 moved run_command's built-in DefaultRunAllowlist from internal/config to internal/tools (its true enforcer, and the direction .agents/rules/60-tools-project-language-generic.md requires - a tool implementation must not depend on the app's own config system): removes the undeclared tools -> config edge and adds the legitimate reverse, config -> tools, for effectiveDiagnosticsAllowlist's validation use. Net edge count unchanged, cap stays at 430. The splash redesign added internal/tui/view/component/welcome -> internal/vcs: welcome reuses internal/vcs's existing no-exec gitdir-pointer resolver to detect the workspace repo/branch for the banner's workspace line, instead of reimplementing that resolver locally. Measured count 413 -> 414, cap stays at 430. The workflow child-run registration seam (Delivery 2) added internal/cli/workflow -> internal/cli/orchestrate: newWorkflowController's register hook closes over the host dispatcher/coordinator/repo and calls cliorchestrate.RegisterChildRunHandle so the standard tools resolve workflow child runs. Measured count 414 -> 415, cap stays at 430. The mouse-selection rewrite added internal/tui/view/select (a leaf under internal/ui: types + highlight engine) with 5 inbound edges (ui/app, ui/component/composer, ui/component/transcript, ui/screen/conversation, ui/screen/transcript), and one newtui -> uikit/termprobe edge for the startup probe. Measured count 415 -> 421, cap stays at 430. The release/v0.2.0 merge unioned this table with the release line's declarations: the internal/chatsync package (edges to events, miviaauth, redact; denied from chat and tools), its consumers (clichat, cliorchestrate, newtui, uiadapter), sdkadapter consumers (cliagents, cliworkflow, subagents), coordinator -> agent, ui/screen/conversation -> ui/component/field; edge cap 430 -> 452."
}
